  "facts": [
    {
      "text": "Existing daycare proposed to increase from 10 to a maximum of 16 children in a split-level house.",
      "locator": "Staff report p.2"
    },
    {
      "text": "Separate Building Approvals application EQ 07-366040 concerned a fire-protection-engineer alternative solution for assembly use.",
      "locator": "Staff report p.3"
    },
    {
      "text": "Proposed measures included limiting use to two lower levels, exit signs, emergency lighting, alarms/detection, exterior exits, and repairs.",
      "locator": "Staff report p.3"
    },
    {
      "text": "Staff said the general approach appeared acceptable, but the alternative solution and building permit had to be completed before the capacity increase.",
      "locator": "Staff report p.3"
    }
  ],
